# Auth Token Infinite Loop Fix — Full Walkthrough

## Root Cause Analysis

The infinite loop after signout was caused by **three compounding issues**:

### 1. Token Key Name Mismatch (Critical)
- **Login** ([index.html](file:///c:/Users/novtw/.gemini/antigravity/index.html)): Stored token in `sessionStorage.setItem('kryptos_token', token)` only
- **Auth check** (`ui.js:32`): Read from `localStorage.getItem('kryptos_token')` FIRST, then `sessionStorage`
- **After page reload**: `sessionStorage` is cleared → token appears missing even though it was valid

### 2. [getAuthHeaders()](file:///c:/Users/novtw/.gemini/antigravity/ui.js#54-70) triggered [clearSession()](file:///c:/Users/novtw/.gemini/antigravity/ui.js#407-536) on missing token
- Every API call (loadProfile, fetchGhostCode, fetchRealData, vault, conversations) called [getAuthHeaders()](file:///c:/Users/novtw/.gemini/antigravity/ui.js#54-70)
- When no token found, it called `UI.clearSession()` via `setTimeout()`
- This created **multiple overlapping [clearSession()](file:///c:/Users/novtw/.gemini/antigravity/ui.js#407-536) calls** — the existing guard `_isClearingSession` reset after 1 second, allowing the next queued call to fire

### 3. No skip for unauthenticated state
- `UI.init()` always called [loadProfile()](file:///c:/Users/novtw/.gemini/antigravity/ui.js#1810-1898), [startGhostCodeWatcher()](file:///c:/Users/novtw/.gemini/antigravity/ui.js#2398-2455), and [fetchRealData()](file:///c:/Users/novtw/.gemini/antigravity/ui.js#726-771) even when no token existed (e.g., fresh page load on the identity screen)
- Each of those made API calls → got 401 → triggered [getAuthHeaders()](file:///c:/Users/novtw/.gemini/antigravity/ui.js#54-70) → triggered [clearSession()](file:///c:/Users/novtw/.gemini/antigravity/ui.js#407-536) loop

---

## Fixes Applied

### Fix 1: Token stored in BOTH storages ([index.html](file:///c:/Users/novtw/.gemini/antigravity/index.html))

**Before** (both login paths):
```js
sessionStorage.setItem('kryptos_token', token);
```

**After**:
```js
sessionStorage.setItem('kryptos_token', token);
localStorage.setItem('kryptos_token', token);
```

This ensures the token survives tab reloads and is always findable by [ui.js](file:///c:/Users/novtw/.gemini/antigravity/ui.js).

---

### Fix 2: [getAuthHeaders()](file:///c:/Users/novtw/.gemini/antigravity/ui.js#54-70) NEVER calls [clearSession()](file:///c:/Users/novtw/.gemini/antigravity/ui.js#407-536) ([ui.js](file:///c:/Users/novtw/.gemini/antigravity/ui.js))

**Before**:
```js
const getAuthHeaders = () => {
    const token = localStorage.getItem('kryptos_token') || sessionStorage.getItem('kryptos_token');
    if (!token) {
        console.warn("[Auth] Token missing or expired. Redirecting to login...");
        setTimeout(() => {
            if (window.UI && UI.clearSession) UI.clearSession();
        }, 100);
        return {};
    }
    return { 'Authorization': `Bearer ${token}`, 'Content-Type': 'application/json' };
};
```

**After**:
```js
function _readToken() {
    return sessionStorage.getItem('kryptos_token')
        || localStorage.getItem('kryptos_token')
        || localStorage.getItem('kryptos_jwt')
        || '';
}

function hasAuthToken() {
    return !!_readToken();
}

const getAuthHeaders = () => {
    const token = _readToken();
    if (!token) return {};  // No side effects — just return empty
    return { 'Authorization': `Bearer ${token}`, 'Content-Type': 'application/json' };
};
```

Key change: [getAuthHeaders()](file:///c:/Users/novtw/.gemini/antigravity/ui.js#54-70) is now a **pure function**. No redirects, no clearSession calls.

---

### Fix 3: One-time guard on [clearSession()](file:///c:/Users/novtw/.gemini/antigravity/ui.js#407-536) ([ui.js](file:///c:/Users/novtw/.gemini/antigravity/ui.js))

**Before**:
```js
clearSession: (isDestroy = false) => {
    if (window._isClearingSession) return;
    window._isClearingSession = true;
    // ... cleanup ...
    setTimeout(() => { window._isClearingSession = false; }, 1000);
},
```

**After**:
```js
let _authRedirectFired = false;  // module-level, permanent per page load

clearSession: (isDestroy = false) => {
    if (_authRedirectFired || window._isClearingSession) return;
    window._isClearingSession = true;
    _authRedirectFired = true;  // PERMANENT — blocks ALL future calls this page load
    // ... cleanup ...
    setTimeout(() => { window._isClearingSession = false; }, 1000);
},
```

`_authRedirectFired` is reset ONLY on the `identity:updated` event (i.e., a successful new login).

---

### Fix 4: Skip API calls when unauthenticated ([ui.js](file:///c:/Users/novtw/.gemini/antigravity/ui.js))

**Before**: `UI.init()` always called [loadProfile()](file:///c:/Users/novtw/.gemini/antigravity/ui.js#1810-1898), [startGhostCodeWatcher()](file:///c:/Users/novtw/.gemini/antigravity/ui.js#2398-2455), etc.

**After**:
```js
if (hasAuthToken()) {
    UI.loadProfile();
}
// ...
if (hasAuthToken()) {
    UI.startGhostCodeWatcher(false);
}
```

Same for [fetchRealData()](file:///c:/Users/novtw/.gemini/antigravity/ui.js#726-771), [fetchGhostCode()](file:///c:/Users/novtw/.gemini/antigravity/ui.js#2366-2397), and [loadProfile()](file:///c:/Users/novtw/.gemini/antigravity/ui.js#1810-1898) — they all now check [hasAuthToken()](file:///c:/Users/novtw/.gemini/antigravity/ui.js#47-53) before making network requests.

---

### Fix 5: `POST /register-node` only fires after valid token ([index.html](file:///c:/Users/novtw/.gemini/antigravity/index.html))

**Before**:
```js
fetch('.../register-node', {
    headers: { 'X-Auth-Token': sessionStorage.getItem('kryptos_token') || '' },
    // ...
});
```

**After**:
```js
const _regToken = sessionStorage.getItem('kryptos_token');
if (_regToken) {
    fetch('.../register-node', {
        headers: { 'Authorization': `Bearer ${_regToken}` },
        // ...
    });
}
```

---

### Fix 6: Debug logging for `POST /auth/node` 400 error ([index.html](file:///c:/Users/novtw/.gemini/antigravity/index.html))

Added payload logging before the fetch:
```js
const authPayload = { nodeId: stored.nodeId };
console.log('[Auth] POST /auth/node payload:', authPayload);
```

And error body logging:
```js
} else {
    console.error('[Auth] /auth/node returned', authRes.status, await authRes.text());
}
```

The 400 error from `/auth/node` occurs when `nodeId` is `undefined` or doesn't match the `0x[hex]` pattern expected by [validateNodeId()](file:///c:/Users/novtw/.gemini/antigravity/kryptos-server.js#170-176). The logging will reveal the actual payload sent.

---

### Fix 7: SignOut clears ONLY session tokens ([ui.js](file:///c:/Users/novtw/.gemini/antigravity/ui.js))

Confirmed the `sessionKeys` list contains only temporary keys:
```js
const sessionKeys = [
    'kryptos_token', 'kryptos_jwt', 'kryptos_node_id',
    'kryptos_vault_unlocked', 'kryptos_session_key', 'kryptos_last_convo'
];
```

Identity keys (`kryptos_identity`, `kryptos_seed_words`, etc.) are ONLY removed when `isDestroy === true` (full identity wipe), never during normal signout.

---

